    "field": "Atlantic climate variability",
    "problem": "The lack of sufficiently long direct observational records of ocean circulation has prevented confirmation of the hypothesized link between ocean circulation and the Atlantic Multidecadal Oscillation (AMO), a key driver of decadal climate variability.",
    "method": "We propose a method using the sea-level difference between tide gauges south and north of Cape Hatteras as a proxy to estimate decadal ocean circulation, thereby providing observational evidence for its role in driving the Atlantic Multidecadal Oscillation.",
    "task": "The task is to use sea-level observations from tide gauges along the US east coast as a proxy for ocean circulation to provide observational evidence for the link between decadal changes in Atlantic circulation and climate variability, specifically the Atlantic Multidecadal Oscillation (AMO).",
